PLACEHOLDER: Celebrating Animation

This is a placeholder for the celebrating celebration animation.
The actual GLB file should contain a 3D skeletal animation with:

Animation Name: celebrating
Duration: 2.0-3.0 seconds
Loop: false (single celebration burst)
FPS: 30

Keyframe Description:
- Frame 0-15: Anticipation - slight crouch, body compresses
- Frame 15-30: Launch - arms raise quickly, body extends upward
- Frame 30-60: Peak celebration - arms fully extended, body at maximum height
- Frame 60-75: Victory pose - arms wave in celebration pattern
- Frame 75-90: Return - gradual return to neutral stance

Bone Hierarchy (standard pet rig):
- Root
  - Spine
    - Chest
      - Head
        - Ears (L/R)
      - Arm_L
        - Hand_L
      - Arm_R
        - Hand_R
    - Tail
  - Leg_L
    - Foot_L
  - Leg_R
    - Foot_R

Expression Channels:
- eyes_wide: 0 -> 1.0 (peak excitement)
- mouth_open: 0 -> 0.8 (happy expression)
- ears_up: 0 -> 1.0 (alert and excited)

Particle Effects (optional):
- Sparkle/confetti effect at peak celebration
- Trail effect on hands during wave

Usage Context:
- Task completion celebration
- Achievement unlocked
- Successful reminder/action execution
- User praise response

Implementation Note:
Since actual GLB binary cannot be created as text, the pet-animation.ts
system will implement this animation procedurally when the GLB file is
not found or invalid. The procedural implementation should:

1. Create upward bounce motion on root bone
2. Animate arms in raising/waving pattern
3. Add slight spin or bounce to body
4. Include ear/tail excitement animation
5. Blend back to idle state smoothly

Reference animations:
- Happy pet celebration in games
- Victory pose from rhythm games
- Achievement unlock animations

Related States in pet-animation.ts:
- celebrating: Main celebration animation
- Triggers: skill_success, task_complete, user_praise
- Transition: celebrating -> idle (after completion)